# Direct dependencies, pinned on 2026-09-02 to the versions the full suite
# passed against (audit section 9 item 15). This file is the source
# pip-compile reads; it is not installed directly and it never ships.
# requirements.txt is the generated artifact: the full dependency closure,
# direct and transitive, pinned to exact versions with hashes (audit
# section 9 item 17), so a Railway build either reproduces this exact set
# or fails outright.
#
# Bump a version here, in its own PR, with the suite and pip-audit green
# on the new set, then regenerate requirements.txt with:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
